[2026-07-08T01:11:54+08:00][sql] INSERT INTO `ai_dev_run_logs` SET `run_id` = 10 , `seq` = 162 , `event_type` = 'assistant' , `content` = '{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"fdf7d0d1-2e5a-488a-8897-b456a2c80fe2\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Here is the complete structural analysis of the project.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Framework\\n\\n**ThinkPHP 5.0.x** (specifically `topthink\\/framework ~5.0.24` via composer.json), based on the [FastAdmin](https:\\/\\/www.fastadmin.net\\/) scaffolding by Karson Zhang.\\n\\n**Key entry points:**\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|---|---|\\n| `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/public\\/index.php` | Main entry point -- loads `APP_PATH` from `..\\/application\\/` and requires `thinkphp\\/start.php` |\\n| `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/public\\/yxAdmin.php` | Admin backend entry point -- binds to the `admin` module, turns off routing |\\n| `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/public\\/router.php` | Dev router -- if file exists serve it, otherwise route to `index.php` |\\n\\nThe composer.json at `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/composer.json` confirms: `\\\"topthink\\/framework\\\": \\\"~5.0.24\\\"`, PHP >= 7.0.0.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. How API Routes Are Defined\\n\\nThere is **one route file**:\\n\\n**`\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/route.php`**\\n\\nIt uses ThinkPHP 5\'s `Route::rule()` method. Example registrations from the file:\\n\\n```php\\nuse \\\\think\\\\Route;\\n\\n\\/\\/ Static image routes with wildcard placeholders\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/static\\/yxkpic\\/fushi\\/:id\\/:year\\/:type\\/:rand\\\", \\\"api\\/compair\\/getFushiPic\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/static\\/yxkpic\\/:type\\/:id\\/:rand\\\",           \\\"api\\/compair\\/getPic\\\");\\n\\n\\/\\/ User target major routes\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/major\\/user-target\\/list\\\",           \\\"api\\/AppMajor\\/targetList\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/major\\/user-target\\/add-or-del\\\",     \\\"api\\/AppMajor\\/addOrDelTarget\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/major\\/user-target\\/index\\\",          \\\"api\\/AppMajor\\/targetIndex\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/major\\/user-target\\/set-default\\\",    \\\"api\\/AppMajor\\/targetSetDefault\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/major\\/user-target\\/1v1\\\",            \\\"api\\/AppMajor\\/target1v1\\\");\\n\\n\\/\\/ Assessment routes\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/user\\/assessment\\\",                  \\\"api\\/User\\/assessmentSubject\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/user\\/set-assessment\\\",              \\\"api\\/User\\/assessmentConf\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/user\\/set-assessment-tiku-score\\\",   \\\"api\\/User\\/assessmentTikuScoreSet\\\");\\nRoute::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/user\\/set-assessment-score\\\",        \\\"api\\/User\\/assessmentScoreSet\\\");\\n```\\n\\n**Pattern:** `Route::rule($url, $route)` where `$route` is `\\\"module\\/controller\\/action\\\"`. For example, `\\\"api\\/AppMajor\\/targetList\\\"` maps to `application\\/api\\/controller\\/AppMajor.php`, method `targetList()`.\\n\\n**Important:** Most API routes do NOT use explicit route registration. In the behavior file `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/common\\/behavior\\/Common.php` (line 15-19), the `appDispatch` hook checks if the URL starts with `api` or `index` and, if so, **turns off route detection** (`\\\\think\\\\App::route(false)`). This means the `api` and `index` modules use **conventional routing** -- the URL path directly maps to `module\\/controller\\/action`. So a request to `\\/api\\/school\\/list` automatically routes to `app\\\\api\\\\controller\\\\School::list()` without needing a route.php entry. Only custom\\/static URLs need explicit routes in `route.php`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. How Controllers Are Organized\\n\\n### Module Structure\\n\\nThe `application\\/` directory contains these modules:\\n\\n```\\napplication\\/\\n  admin\\/          -- Admin backend controllers, models, views\\n    controller\\/\\n      auth\\/       -- Admin, Group, Rule, Adminlog\\n      general\\/    -- Profile, Config, Attachment\\n      Category.php, Dashboard.php, School.php, Major.php, ...\\n    model\\/\\n    validate\\/\\n    view\\/\\n  api\\/            -- REST API controllers (your focus)\\n    controller\\/   -- All API endpoint controllers\\n    logic\\/        -- Business logic layer\\n    library\\/      -- ExceptionHandle, ComErrorDescs\\n    validate\\/     -- Parameter validation classes\\n  common\\/         -- Shared across other modules\\n    controller\\/   -- Base controller classes (Api, ApiAuth, Backend, Frontend)\\n    model\\/        -- Shared models\\n    behavior\\/     -- Hooks (Common behavior)\\n    library\\/      -- Auth, Token\\n  index\\/          -- Front-facing web module\\n    controller\\/\\n  task\\/           -- Background\\/cron controllers\\n  extra\\/          -- Additional config files\\n```\\n\\n### API Controllers\\n\\nLocated at `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/api\\/controller\\/`:\\n\\n```\\nAi.php, Analysis.php, AppMajor.php, Base.php, ChooseSchool.php,\\nChooseSchoolV3.php, Compair.php, Course.php, Fushi.php, Gather.php,\\nIndex.php, Major.php, MajorSchool.php, NewsFlash.php, Pick.php,\\nPlan.php, Roster.php, School.php, Score.php, Search.php, Test.php,\\nUser.php, YearDetail.php, Yuanxi.php\\n```\\n\\n### Example API Controller Pattern\\n\\nTaking `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/api\\/controller\\/School.php`:\\n\\n```php\\nnamespace app\\\\api\\\\controller;\\n\\nuse app\\\\common\\\\controller\\\\ApiAuth;   \\/\\/ <-- Extends API base with auth\\n\\/\\/ ... use statements\\n\\nclass School extends ApiAuth\\n{\\n    \\/\\/ Actions that bypass authentication entirely\\n    protected $noNeedLogin = [\'*\'];\\n\\n    \\/\\/ Actions that need login but not permission checks\\n    protected $noNeedRight = [\'*\'];\\n\\n    public function _initialize()\\n    {\\n        parent::_initialize();\\n        $this->model = model(\'School\');   \\/\\/ <-- Model loading\\n    }\\n\\n    \\/\\/ Public methods = API endpoints\\n    public function filter() { ... $this->success(\'success\', $filter); }\\n    public function list()   { ... $this->success(\'success\', $data); }\\n    public function index()  { ... $this->success(\'success\', $data); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Key Patterns Observed Across All API Controllers:\\n\\n1. **Three possible base classes:**\\n   - `app\\\\common\\\\controller\\\\ApiAuth` (most API controllers use this) -- full auth with sign verification\\n   - `app\\\\common\\\\controller\\\\Api` -- older\\/lighter auth (login + token only)\\n   - `app\\\\common\\\\controller\\\\Frontend` -- for the `index` module\\n\\n2. **Access control properties:**\\n   - `$noNeedLogin` -- array of action names (or `[\'*\']` for all) that don\'t require login\\n   - `$noNeedRight` -- array of actions that don\'t need permission\\/role checks\\n   - `$needVpn` -- (in `ApiAuth`) actions that require VPN\\/whitelist checks\\n\\n3. **Standard response helpers:**\\n   - `$this->success($msg, $data)` -- returns `{errno: 0, success: 1000, data: {...}, msg: \\\"success\\\"}`\\n   - `$this->error($msg, $data, $code)` -- returns error response\\n\\n4. **Input retrieval:** `input(\'param_name\', \'default_value\')` -- ThinkPHP 5 helper\\n\\n5. **Model usage:** Direct `Db::connect(\'database.yx_db_config\')->name(\'cl_school\')->where(...)->select()` or model instances (`$this->model->where(...)->select()`)\\n\\n### Inheritance Chain\\n\\n```\\nApiAuth (application\\/common\\/controller\\/ApiAuth.php)\\n  |\\n  +-- app\\\\api\\\\controller\\\\Base      (has getConfig, getCompanyWechat)\\n  +-- app\\\\api\\\\controller\\\\School    (filter, list, index, introduce, zsjzList)\\n  +-- app\\\\api\\\\controller\\\\Major     (yxFind, yxList, filter, list, info, collect, ...)\\n  +-- app\\\\api\\\\controller\\\\Search    (index, schoolList, majorList, feedback, ...)\\n  +-- app\\\\api\\\\controller\\\\User\\n  +-- ... (most API controllers)\\n\\nApi (application\\/common\\/controller\\/Api.php)\\n  |\\n  +-- (older API controllers, less commonly used now)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Middleware \\/ Parameter Validation\\n\\n**There is no ThinkPHP 5 middleware** (this version predates the middleware concept introduced in ThinkPHP 5.1). Instead, validation is handled through two mechanisms:\\n\\n### A. ThinkPHP Validate Classes\\n\\nLocated at `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/api\\/validate\\/`:\\n\\n```\\nAuth.php\\nAi.php\\nChooseSchool.php\\n```\\n\\nAnd at `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/admin\\/validate\\/`:\\n\\n```\\nAdmin.php, AuthRule.php, Category.php, Command.php, Platform.php,\\nUser.php, UserGroup.php, UserRule.php, Version.php,\\ngeneral\\/Attachment.php, TClRoster.php, ImportRecord.php\\n```\\n\\n**Example -- `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/api\\/validate\\/ChooseSchool.php`:**\\n\\n```php\\nnamespace app\\\\api\\\\validate;\\n\\nuse think\\\\Validate;\\n\\nclass ChooseSchool extends Validate\\n{\\n    protected $rule = [\\n        \'now_standing\'  => \'require|checkNowStanding\',\\n        \'school_id\'     => \'require\',\\n        \'major_name\'    => \'require\',\\n        \\/\\/ ...\\n    ];\\n\\n    protected $message = [\\n        \'now_standing\'  => ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM.\',当前状态\',\\n        \\/\\/ ...\\n    ];\\n\\n    protected $scene = [\\n        \'get_score\'  => [\'now_standing\', \'school_id\', \'major_name\', ...],\\n        \'get_count\'  => [\'area_id\', \'school_attr\', \'major_id\', \'is_full\'],\\n    ];\\n\\n    \\/\\/ Custom validation methods\\n    public function checkNowStanding($value) { ... }\\n    public function checkSchoolAttr($value) { ... }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nControllers call validation via `$this->validate($data, \'ValidateName.scene\')` (the method is inherited from `Api` base class at line 268 of `Api.php`).\\n\\n### B. Header\\/Signature Validation (Built into ApiAuth base class)\\n\\nIn `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/common\\/controller\\/ApiAuth.php` (`_initialize()`, lines 87-166), every API request that requires auth goes through:\\n\\n- Parameter extraction: `sign`, `signTime`, `platform`, `version`, `nonce`, `appId`\\n- `$this->auth->checkAuth()` -- validates the digital signature\\n- `$this->auth->isLogin()` -- checks token-based login status\\n\\nThe `api\\/validate\\/Auth.php` class is a standalone validator that lives in `app\\\\api\\\\validate\\\\Auth` but active validation of header params happens inline in the `ApiAuth` base controller, not as separate middleware.\\n\\n### C. Behavior Hooks (Tags)\\n\\nDefined in `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/tags.php`, behaviors are registered on lifecycle events (app_init, app_begin, module_init, action_begin). The `Common` behavior in `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/common\\/behavior\\/Common.php` handles URL routing logic as described above.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Project Architecture (MVC)\\n\\nThis is a **modular MVC architecture** built on the FastAdmin (ThinkPHP 5) framework. The structure is genuinely Model-View-Controller:\\n\\n| Layer | Location | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Model** | `application\\/{module}\\/model\\/`, `application\\/common\\/model\\/` | Eloquent-like ORM (ThinkPHP models). Some API controllers bypass models entirely and use `Db::connect()` directly. |\\n| **View** | `application\\/admin\\/view\\/`, `application\\/index\\/view\\/`, `application\\/common\\/view\\/` | Template files (`.html`). API module has no views -- it returns JSON. |\\n| **Controller** | `application\\/{module}\\/controller\\/` | Entry points, request handling, response. |\\n| **Logic** | `application\\/api\\/logic\\/` | Thin business-logic layer used by some API controllers. |\\n| **Validate** | `application\\/{module}\\/validate\\/` | Input validation classes. |\\n| **Library** | `application\\/common\\/library\\/`, `application\\/api\\/library\\/` | Shared services (Auth, Token, ExceptionHandle). |\\n\\n**Module isolation**: The project has 5 major modules:\\n\\n- **`index`** -- Public web pages (conventional routing, views returned)\\n- **`api`** -- JSON API endpoints (conventional routing, no views)  \\n- **`admin`** -- Admin backend (conventional routing via `yxAdmin.php`, views returned)\\n- **`common`** -- Shared base classes, models, and behaviors\\n- **`task`** -- Background\\/cron job controllers\\n\\n**Request lifecycle for an API call** (e.g., `\\/api\\/school\\/list`):\\n\\n1. `public\\/index.php` -- loads framework\\n2. ThinkPHP route detection applied\\n3. `app\\\\common\\\\behavior\\\\Common::appDispatch()` -- disables route matching for `api` prefix\\n4. Conventional routing resolves to `app\\\\api\\\\controller\\\\School` class\\n5. Controller constructor runs -> `_initialize()` from `ApiAuth` base class:\\n   - CORS check\\n   - Input filtering (trim, strip_tags, htmlspecialchars)\\n   - Signature validation (if auth required)\\n   - Token login check\\n   - VPN whitelist check (if configured)\\n6. Action method executes (`list()`)\\n7. Response via `$this->success()` \\/ `$this->error()`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary for Adding a Bubble Sort API Endpoint\\n\\nBased on this exploration, here is what you need to follow:\\n\\n- **Route**: Add to `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/route.php` using `Route::rule(\\\"\\/api\\/bubble-sort\\/...\\\", \\\"api\\/YourController\\/yourAction\\\");` -- OR rely on conventional routing (just the controller\\/action path works).\\n\\n- **Controller**: Create under `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/api\\/controller\\/`. Extend `app\\\\common\\\\controller\\\\ApiAuth` (or `Api` if no auth needed). Set `$noNeedLogin = [\'*\']` and `$noNeedRight = [\'*\']` if it\'s an open endpoint.\\n\\n- **Validation**: Optionally create a validate class under `\\/Users\\/hufangfang\\/www\\/local\\/yuanxiao\\/application\\/api\\/validate\\/`.\\n\\n- **Response**: Use `$this->success($msg, $data)` and `$this->error($msg, $data, $code)` inherited from the base class.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2219,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":59392,\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":\"call_00_aQPH51Kq0V2SHHCt5Wim9371\",\"session_id\":\"709785dc-e16e-484f-9922-07c4f799ccb4\",\"uuid\":\"97e2bf4d-374a-41c8-b630-448a38b3e2ad\",\"subagent_type\":\"Explore\",\"task_description\":\"Explore project structure for API dev plan\"}' , `created_at` = '2026-07-08 01:11:54' [ RunTime:0.003109s ]
