hey fail, they should return an error string in the same format: `ERROR_CODE,field_description`.\\n\\nNow let me also consider: in the scenario `sort`, when `nums` is missing (not provided at all), the `require` rule will trigger and use the message `EC_MISSING_PARAM.\',\'.nums` → `160006,nums`.\\n\\nWhen `nums` is provided but not an array, the `array` rule will trigger. I need a message for that. Looking at the ChooseSchool example, each field only has one message. But in TP5, you can specify messages for specific rules using `field.rule` format.\\n\\nActually, looking more carefully at the ChooseSchool example, the message only has one entry per field. And in TP5, a single message for a field covers all rules. So the first failed rule will use that message.\\n\\nWait, that\'s not great for distinguishing between \\\"missing\\\" and \\\"invalid\\\". Let me think about this differently.\\n\\nFor the `require` rule, if the field is missing, it returns the message. For `array`, if it\'s not an array, it returns the message.\\n\\nIn TP5, you can specify messages per rule: `\'nums.require\' => ...`, `\'nums.array\' => ...`, `\'nums.checkNotEmptyArray\' => ...`\\n\\nBut looking at the existing code, they use a single message per field. Let me follow the same pattern but provide rule-specific messages for better error reporting.\\n\\nActually, I think I should follow the existing pattern. Looking at the plan:\\n\\n> 定义 `$message`：使用 `ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM`、`EC_INVALID_PARAM`、`EC_EMPTY_PARAM` 作为错误码\\n\\nLet me use the TP5 convention with field.rule format for messages to give proper error codes:\\n\\n```php\\nprotected $message = [\\n    \'nums.require\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM . \',nums\',\\n    \'nums.array\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_INVALID_PARAM . \',nums\',\\n    \'nums.checkNotEmptyArray\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_EMPTY_PARAM . \',nums\',\\n];\\n```\\n\\nWait, but the plan says to use the format like ChooseSchool. Let me look at it more carefully.\\n\\nIn ChooseSchool, the message has keys like `\'now_standing\'` and values like `ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM.\',\'.\'当前状态\'`. This single message covers all validation rules for that field.\\n\\nFor BubbleSort, since we have different error types (missing vs invalid vs empty), it makes sense to use field.rule format. Let me use that approach to be more precise while still following the project\'s error code convention.\\n\\nActually, let me just follow the simple pattern from the plan more closely. The plan says:\\n> 定义 `$message`：使用 `ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM`、`EC_INVALID_PARAM`、`EC_EMPTY_PARAM` 作为错误码\\n\\nI\'ll do it like:\\n```php\\nprotected $message = [\\n    \'nums.require\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM . \',nums\',\\n    \'nums.array\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_INVALID_PARAM . \',nums\',  \\n    \'nums.checkNotEmptyArray\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_EMPTY_PARAM . \',nums\',\\n];\\n```\\n\\nNow let me create all the files.\",\"signature\":\"a53451f1-126d-4c74-9733-3cae158d4bbe\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":558,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36992,\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"37dc5757-0222-4939-8ad9-8622b84ce140\",\"uuid\":\"92de21aa-ff4c-498b-b897-fd159a216609\"}
